---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { about } from "../content";
import PageHero from "@dst/ui/PageHero.astro";
---
<Layout
  prose title={about.title} description={about.description}>
  <PageHero
    title={about.h1}
    image="/covers/about.jpg"
    imageAlt="Cut-paper illustration: a street grid of narrow blocks crossed by one long diagonal avenue."
    imageKind="generated"
  >
    <p class="lede">{about.lede}</p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p set:html={`<strong>nyc42.lol</strong> covers New York City &mdash; museums and theatre, the river and the parks, and the things the seasons open and close. What is on, what changed, and when.`} />
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The rules</h2>
    <ol class="rules">
      <li>
        <h3>Every fact names where it came from, and when we last looked</h3>
        <p>Not &ldquo;updated regularly&rdquo;. A source and a date, printed on the entry itself, so you can see how fresh the thing you are reading actually is.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Nothing is listed on a date we could not confirm</h3>
        <p>Dates come from the organiser, not from another listings page. An event whose date we could not confirm waits until we can.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>What&rsquo;s on, not what went wrong</h3>
        <p>This site covers what is happening, what is open and what changed for the better. Not politics, not crime, not tragedy, and not arguments. If a story needs a side taken, it belongs somewhere that can follow it up.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>We pick the best, and say why</h3>
        <p>A listings site earns its keep by choosing. Picking out the best of something is the job, not a compromise &mdash; what it will not do is run a place down. A takedown of a named business is not what this is for.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A page exists when there is something to put on it</h3>
        <p>No empty sections waiting to be filled, and no index padded out to look busy. A section appears once there is something on it.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .rules {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: rule;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .rules li {
    counter-increment: rule;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr;
    gap: 0 var(--space-2);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .rules li::before {
    content: counter(rule);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .rules h3 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .rules p { margin: 0.25em 0 0; grid-column: 2; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--ink-muted); }
</style>
